  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "During the turtleback wolf assault on Ge tribe’s migrating camp in Northern Plains, Ge tribe leader commands Ge Cui, Ge Xiang, and Ge Mi to lead the first, seventh, and eighteenth troop respectively, stop their current tasks, and dig a canal from the riverside so river water can help the defense. The same order assigns the third, fifth, and sixteenth troop to take over those unfinished tasks. Fang Yuan, under the Wolf King name Chang Shan Yin, had just proposed drawing the river to the camp because the tribe could not move its mortals to the riverside in time.",
